course: dictionary
lesson: 14722
title: Professionally: paid, skilled, or expert
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone does something. «Professionally» is one of them. It comes from the word professional, and it has a few meanings, so look at the clues around it.
explain: It can mean someone does something as a paid job, not just as a hobby. «She sings professionally» tells you singing is her job, and people pay her for it.
explain: It can also mean doing something in a calm, skilled, polite way, as a good worker should. «He handled the angry customer professionally» means he stayed calm and polite, even though the customer was cross.
explain: Look for clues. Is there money or a job nearby? Then it means paid. Is there a high standard or careful skill? Then it means expert or polished. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
fact: Professionally is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Professionally» can mean as a paid job, in a skilled and polite way, or by an expert.
fact: «Professionally trained» means taught by experts to a high standard.
fact: «Behave professionally» means act calmly, politely, and like a good worker.
fact: The words around «professionally» are the clues that show which meaning fits.
exercise: «Tom plays football professionally for a club.» What does professionally mean here? | In a messy way | As a hobby on Sunday mornings | Very slowly | *As a paid job
exercise: «The shop assistant dealt with the rude man professionally.» What does professionally suggest? | In a loud, angry way | Without any care | By accident | *In a calm, polite, skilled way
exercise: Find the word in «The cake was professionally decorated» that tells you it was done by an expert. | cake | *professionally | was | decorated
test: Ella says «She sings professionally» means she only sings at home for fun. What does it really mean? | *She sings as her paid job, not just for fun | She sings only at home for fun | She sings very quietly | She sings in the rain
test: «The team behaved professionally after losing the match.» What does professionally mean here? | For money only | In a loud and rude way | *In a calm, good, sporting way | Very quickly
exam: «The photos were professionally taken, so they look sharp and clear.» Why do the photos look so good? | They were taken in the dark | *They were taken by skilled experts | They were taken by a child with a toy camera | They were taken by accident
